      "writtenOn": "2023-06-14T17:30:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The actual process is a bit more complex than this. I don\u0027t know how close to the real thing you\u0027ll need to get, but `tc_perform_snk_hard_reset` manages the timers involved in the Hard Reset process. To cover it thoroughly, I think the test would probably need some awareness of those timers as well. I think the partner emulator probably does this incorrectly in general, but we get away with it, because we end up resetting anyway.\n\nThe process is described in PD r3.1 v1.8 ss 7.3.4.1 Source Initiated Hard Reset. Hopefully, you won\u0027t need to refer to that. https://usb.org/document-library/usb-power-delivery\n\n1. Partner sends the Hard Reset. You\u0027re already doing this.\n2. Partner waits ~30 ms.\n3. Partner drops to vSafe0V. You\u0027re already doing this, but too early. The max time for this is 650 ms. I don\u0027t think you need to worry about the minimum time, but you could make it like 20 ms for plausibility.\n4. Partner waits between 660 and 1000 ms.\n5. Partner turns back on VBUS to vSafe5V. Again, there\u0027s a max amount of time for this of 275 ms but no min time.\n\n3 is the step that covers the code you\u0027re trying to cover.",
      "revId": "f03d55c5d52c56dc71fc40ade579a8ff3e3d4f41",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
